        <!-- =====================================================
             Presto SQL Parser Dependency (Optional for Native API Mode)
             =====================================================
             
             To enable Presto native parsing (Route B), add one of the following:
             
             Option 1: Use official PrestoSQL parser (recommended for production)
             ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
             <dependency>
                 <groupId>io.prestosql</groupId>
                 <artifactId>presto-parser</artifactId>
                 <version>372</version>
                 <scope>provided</scope>
             </dependency>
             
             Note: Version 372 is compatible with PrestoDB 0.260+
             Check available versions at: 
             https://repo.maven.apache.org/maven2/io/prestosql/presto-parser/
             
             Option 2: Use Superior Presto parser (already added below)
             ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
             Already included via superior-presto-parser:4.0.16
             
             How to enable:
             ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
             1. Uncomment the dependency above
             2. Run: mvn clean install
             3. PrestoSQLLineageExtractor will automatically detect and use it
             4. Check logs for "Presto parser available" message
             
             Graceful Degradation:
             ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
             If dependency is missing, PrestoSQLLineageExtractor will:
             - Log a warning about missing parser
             - Automatically fall back to TEXT_PARSING mode
             - Continue working with JSQLParser-based text parsing
             
             Reference: See PrestoParserManager.java for implementation details
             ===================================================== -->

